WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.800
Woke.

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.402
Here is how Merriam

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.704
Webster's Dictionary describes it.

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.673
Aware of and actively attentive

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.375
to important societal facts,

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.276
especially issues of racial

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.745
and social justice.

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.213
Now, it's a word that we all hear

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.681
a lot of these days.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.583
And Wolk was coined by black activists

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:18.251
to bring attention to racial injustice.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:20.220
But these days, conservatives

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.355
are working overtime to redefine it,

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.190
to suit their political ends,

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:24.624
so much

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:25.992
so that it may very well

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:28.194
have lost all of its meaning.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.162
Take, for example,

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.997
this noted conservative

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:31.798
who this week

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:32.766
struggled to come up

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:35.001
with her own definition

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:36.836
Would you mind defining?

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:37.504
Well, because it's come up

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:38.071
a couple of times.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:38.705
I just want to make sure

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.740
we're on the same page.

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:43.877
So, I mean, Woke is

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.613
sort of the idea that

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:52.185
I

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.954
this is going to be one of those moments

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:55.622
that goes viral.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.589
I mean, Wolk

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.324
is something that's very hard to define.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.759
And we've spent an entire chapter

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.194
defining it.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.896
It is sort of the understanding

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.364
that we need to retool,

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:07.033
totally reimagine and

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.101
redo society

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:08.935
in order to create

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:12.872
hierarchies of oppression.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.476
So I it's hard to explain

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:19.412
in a 15 second soundbite.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:20.580
And she was absolutely right.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.048
It did go viral.

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:24.584
But beyond that viral moment,

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:25.752
the issue

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.420
actually is what she said at the end,

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.088
which is

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:31.458
how complicated is it to define Wolk?

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:32.792
Here's

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:33.960
her follow up tweet

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.829
explaining her actual definition.

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:36.496
She says,

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.831
It's a radical belief system

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.232
suggesting that our institutions

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.101
are built around discrimination

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:41.801
and claiming

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:42.936
that all disparity

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.604
is a result of that discrimination.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:45.271
It seeks

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.507
a radical redefinition of society

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.910
in which equality of group result is

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.980
the endpoint enforced by an angry mob.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.682
Now, to me,

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.550
one of the issues here isn't so much

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.285
that she couldn't do it in that moment.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:01:59.853
It's really

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.187
that the definition

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.889
that she's putting forward

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:03.823
is one

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:04.290
that has

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.559
been created by conservatives

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.161
in the last couple of

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:08.661
I mean, let's

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.296
call it 18 to 20 months

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.398
since the summer of 20, 20

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.000
And it's been created

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:14.434
in order

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.301
to sort of attack

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.670
the idea of social injustice

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.606
as a concept, it seems

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.141
I always understood.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.243
Well initially when this term came about,

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:25.345
I understood to be understanding

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.713
our nation's history

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:29.482
to inform us about societal barriers.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:30.884
Currently

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:31.584
it seems,

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.620
however, that sort of become a catchall

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:36.856
to form certain politicians to appeal

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.124
to the grievances

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:40.627
and anger of certain voters.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.862
In times that are convenient to those

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:43.730
certain politicians.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:47.167
I've heard it in debates ranging

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.968
from why

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:49.802
certain topics

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.638
shouldn't be taught in classrooms

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.706
to why certain banks have failed

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.275
in the past couple of weeks.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:58.211
Which to me says that you are kind

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.846
of picking and choosing this word

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.614
for when it's convenient to you.

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.283
I want to bring Ramesh in on this

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.617
because I,

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:05.718
I understand

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.320
that you are probably more sympathetic

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.756
to Bethany's definition

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.724
then than some other people might be.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.326
But I think the question is

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:15.895
if it's so hard to define.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.964
Does it just kind of come to mean

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.766
whatever anybody wants it to mean?

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:20.133
Well,

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:20.934
that's the nature

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.502
of a lot of political terms, right?

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.270
I mean, conservatism and liberalism

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.371
or ultra maga

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.973
Republicanism, as President Biden

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:27.707
likes to say,

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.242
all of these things are sort of fuzzy

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:29.976
concepts

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:30.476
and different

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.078
people are going to give you different

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.313
definitions of it.

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.348
I do think that we should try

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.317
to be as precise as possible

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.986
when we're arguing about a specific thing

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.721
to talk about that specific thing

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:42.722
and not to go straight

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:44.490
to this abstract term.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.692
I think, though, that

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:48.595
that the the general phenomenon here

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.130
that people who are complaining

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:51.698
about wokeness

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:53.766
or talking about is an actual turn

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.034
that has happened

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.237
on the left side of our politics

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.771
towards a heightened sensitivity

00:03:58.771 --> 00:03:59.372
of course.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:01.374
There's such a thing as oversensitivity,

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:03.209
and that's what the criticism

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.477
generally amounts to.

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:06.079
And to your point about

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.948
kind of the specificity or lack thereof,

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:11.651
I just want to play for a little bit

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.052
what we're talking about when this

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.354
we talk about a buzzword.

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:15.154
I mean, this has become

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.322
the ultimate buzzword

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:19.125
on the 20, 24 campaign trail

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:20.927
We will end work.

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.462
I think it goes back to this Woke

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:23.363
Mind virus

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:25.365
that's infected the left

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.200
and all these other institutions.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:27.934
This work

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:30.303
self loathing has swept our country.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.671
It's in the classroom,

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:32.872
the boardroom, in the back

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:33.740
rooms of government.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.141
He's the first man

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:38.578
to surrender his presidency to a woke mob

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:41.014
that can't even tell you what a woman is.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.650
So putting aside the definition

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:44.450
for a second.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.853
That to me says

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:48.888
as we're moving forward toward 2024.

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:50.523
This is going to be a central component

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.057
of that race.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:53.226
Oh, absolutely. And it already is. Right.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:54.394
As you were saying,

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:56.129
it has become very much

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:58.364
this catchall pejorative term

00:04:58.364 --> 00:04:59.532
that conservatives

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:00.967
in particular like to use.

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:02.535
And particularly

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:03.469
when there's even

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.238
just like a whiff of an issue

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.539
having to do

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:08.007
with race or gender

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:10.109
or sexual orientation,

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:12.945
inclusivity, diversity issues.

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:14.747
Republicans in particular

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:16.316
have been using the term to go

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:18.418
after liberals and Democrats

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:19.686
whenever they feel like

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:21.120
there is a situation

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.922
where they're sort of trying to meddle

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.190
in your personal life. Right.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.124
So, you know,

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:26.626
they're trying to teach our children

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:27.860
this or make our children

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.962
eat this in at schools.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:30.997
So, yeah,

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:32.699
it is definitely going to be

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:34.934
a hugely defining

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:36.803
sort of tool

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:38.771
that Republicans use heading into 20, 20,

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:41.040
so that my curiosity will be

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.575
as we go toward 20, 24.

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:43.242
Once this gets

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:45.445
beyond the Republican primary,

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:46.946
what do real people

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:48.147
who are living their lives

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:49.182
think about this?

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.550
Are they waking up in the morning

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:51.351
and thinking, wow,

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:53.186
my kid's school is too woke?

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:54.821
I think that that's

00:05:54.821 --> 00:05:56.122
just an open question.

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:57.390
I don't have an answer to it,

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.158
but we'll see how that turns out.

